WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.716 --> 00:00:15.298
can I go over and see Diana just for a minute?"

2
00:00:15.778 --> 00:00:16.339
asked Anne.

3
00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:20.141
"I don't want you going out after dark," said Marilla.

4
00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:24.204
"But she has something important to tell me," cried Anne.

5
00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.545
"How do you know?"

6
00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:28.548
"Because she just signaled me from her window.

7
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.803
We make flashes with the candle by waving cardboard in front.

8
00:00:33.423 --> 00:00:34.904
It was my idea, Marilla!"

9
00:00:34.924 --> 00:00:38.527
"That doesn't surprise me, Anne," Marilla replied.

10
00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:42.209
Anne dashed over to Diana's and dashed back.

11
00:00:42.229 --> 00:00:43.790
"Oh, Marilla!

12
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.612
You know that tomorrow is Diana's birthday?

13
00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:52.196
Well, she asked me to stay at her house, in the guest room!

14
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:59.385
Her cousins are coming with a big sleigh, and we are all going to the Debating Club concert—if

15
00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.926
you'll let me go, that is.

16
00:01:01.526 --> 00:01:03.147
You will, won't you?"

17
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.129
"No, you can't go.

18
00:01:05.949 --> 00:01:09.692
Little girls should not go to concerts at night," Marilla said.

19
00:01:10.813 --> 00:01:13.915
Anne, with tears rolling down her cheeks, went upstairs.

20
00:01:14.735 --> 00:01:17.197
Meanwhile Matthew slept on the sofa.

21
00:01:17.818 --> 00:01:23.021
Matthew opened his eyes and said, "Marilla, I think Anne should go to the concert."

22
00:01:23.721 --> 00:01:24.942
He had not been asleep.

23
00:01:24.962 --> 00:01:28.463
"Well, I don't," snorted Marilla.

24
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:31.185
"Who's bringing up Anne, you or me?"

25
00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:33.726
"You are," admitted Matthew.

26
00:01:34.366 --> 00:01:38.828
But he kept asking, and eventually Marilla let Anne go to the concert.

27
00:01:39.809 --> 00:01:45.711
On the day of the concert, Diana did Anne's hair in the new style, and Anne tied Diana's

28
00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:47.072
bows in a special way.

29
00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:54.019
Anne felt a little sad when she compared her plain black dress and shapeless coat with Diana's pretty

30
00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:55.920
green dress and smart jacket.

31
00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.501
But Anne remembered she had an imagination and she could use it.

32
00:02:01.682 --> 00:02:06.664
Early in the evening, Diana's cousins arrived, and they crowded into the big sleigh.

33
00:02:07.364 --> 00:02:12.967
As they drove through the snow, there were tinkles of sleigh bells, and the night seemed magical to

34
00:02:13.107 --> 00:02:15.448
Anne. The concert was thrilling too.

35
00:02:16.208 --> 00:02:21.489
Only one item on the program failed to interest her—Gilbert Blythe reciting a poem.

36
00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.451
Anne picked up a book and read it until he finished, but Diana clapped and clapped for the

37
00:02:27.491 --> 00:02:32.332
performer. It was eleven o'clock when they got home, and the house was silent.

38
00:02:33.053 --> 00:02:35.453
Anne and Diana tiptoed into the guest room.

39
00:02:35.473 --> 00:02:37.234
"Are you ready for bed?"

40
00:02:37.614 --> 00:02:38.214
Anne asked.

41
00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.475
"Let's race to the bed!"

42
00:02:41.095 --> 00:02:44.376
The two girls ran and jumped on the bed in the spare room.

43
00:02:45.076 --> 00:02:47.417
And then something moved under them.

44
00:02:48.018 --> 00:02:55.484
There was a gasp and a cry, and somebody said in a muffled voice, "Oh my goodness!"

45
00:02:56.865 --> 00:02:59.727
Anne and Diana dashed out of the room and up the stairs.

46
00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:02.229
It was cold and they were shivering.

47
00:03:02.249 --> 00:03:03.810
"Who was it?

48
00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.492
What was it?"

49
00:03:06.032 --> 00:03:06.793
whispered Anne.

50
00:03:06.813 --> 00:03:09.995
"Oh, Anne, it was Aunt Josephine.

51
00:03:10.676 --> 00:03:13.058
She'll be furious," answered Diana.

52
00:03:13.078 --> 00:03:15.700
"Who's Aunt Josephine?"

53
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.903
"She's my father's aunt, and she lives in Charlottetown.

54
00:03:20.544 --> 00:03:25.247
She's really old—seventy—and I don't think she was ever young.

55
00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:28.150
She's very strict," Diana said.

56
00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.033
Miss Josephine Barry did not appear at breakfast the next morning.

57
00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:36.256
Mrs. Barry smiled kindly at the two girls.

58
00:03:36.276 --> 00:03:38.958
"Did you have a good time last night?

59
00:03:39.559 --> 00:03:44.402
I meant to tell you that Aunt Josephine came and stayed in the guest room, but I was

60
00:03:44.543 --> 00:03:46.004
so tired I fell asleep."

61
00:03:46.736 --> 00:03:49.237
Diana and Anne just smiled at each other.

62
00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:53.460
Anne went home after breakfast, and then later went to Mrs.

63
00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.921
Lynde's house on an errand.

64
00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:59.543
"So you nearly frightened Miss Barry to death last night?"

65
00:03:59.983 --> 00:04:00.524
said Mrs.

66
00:04:00.584 --> 00:04:03.745
Lynde. "Diana's mother is very upset.

67
00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:10.049
Josephine Barry came to stay for a month, but she changed her mind and is leaving tomorrow!

68
00:04:10.829 --> 00:04:15.332
And she had promised to pay for Diana's piano lessons, but now she isn't.

69
00:04:16.156 --> 00:04:18.377
She thinks Diana is a tomboy.

70
00:04:19.117 --> 00:04:23.299
Old Miss Barry is rich, and the Barrys want to keep on her good side.

71
00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:26.300
Anne, you should look before you leap.

72
00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.481
Especially into beds!"

73
00:04:29.642 --> 00:04:33.863
Mrs. Lynde laughed at her own joke, but Anne saw nothing to laugh at.

74
00:04:34.664 --> 00:04:36.304
Anne went back and saw Diana.

75
00:04:36.324 --> 00:04:42.267
"Anne, after you left, Aunt Josephine woke up and she was so angry!

76
00:04:43.007 --> 00:04:48.042
She won't stay, and I don't care, but Mother and Father do," said Diana.

77
00:04:48.643 --> 00:04:51.245
"Diana, didn't you say it was my fault?"

78
00:04:51.785 --> 00:04:52.366
asked Anne.

79
00:04:52.386 --> 00:04:54.647
"I'm no tattletale, Anne!

80
00:04:55.348 --> 00:04:56.549
It was my fault too."

81
00:04:56.569 --> 00:05:02.094
"Well, I'm going to tell Aunt Josephine myself," Anne announced.

82
00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.375
Diana stared.

83
00:05:04.395 --> 00:05:05.977
"Anne Shirley!

84
00:05:05.997 --> 00:05:09.019
Why why, she'll eat you alive!"

85
00:05:09.039 --> 00:05:11.181
"I must, Diana.

86
00:05:11.201 --> 00:05:14.624
It was my fault and I've got to confess.

87
00:05:15.336 --> 00:05:18.098
Luckily, I've had practice at confessions."

88
00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:21.100
Aunt Josephine was knitting by the fire.

89
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.741
"Who are you?"

90
00:05:23.241 --> 00:05:23.962
she demanded.

91
00:05:23.982 --> 00:05:29.966
"I'm Anne of Green Gables," said the small visitor, "and I've come to confess."

92
00:05:29.986 --> 00:05:31.807
"Confess what?"

93
00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:33.228
Miss Barry asked.

94
00:05:33.248 --> 00:05:37.931
"It was my idea that Diana and I jump on your bed.

95
00:05:38.532 --> 00:05:44.536
Diana is a very ladylike girl, and it's not fair to blame her," Anne said.

96
00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:48.101
"Diana jumped too," said Miss Barry.

97
00:05:48.121 --> 00:05:52.023
"It was just for fun," persisted Anne.

98
00:05:52.043 --> 00:05:55.625
"Diana really wants to learn the piano.

99
00:05:55.645 --> 00:05:59.326
If you must be angry, be angry with me.

100
00:06:00.047 --> 00:06:01.267
Mrs. Hammond and Mrs.

101
00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.388
Thomas were always angry at me.

102
00:06:04.089 --> 00:06:07.890
I am used to it, and I can endure it better than Diana."

103
00:06:08.991 --> 00:06:11.312
The old lady was not angry anymore.

104
00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.782
In fact, she was interested in this strange redheaded girl.

105
00:06:15.802 --> 00:06:19.885
"Two girls bounced on me in the middle of the night!"

106
00:06:20.385 --> 00:06:21.426
she said sternly.

107
00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:24.207
"You don't know what it was like."

108
00:06:24.227 --> 00:06:29.210
"I don't know, but I can imagine," Anne said eagerly.

109
00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:32.072
"It must have been very disturbing.

110
00:06:32.612 --> 00:06:35.114
Do you have any imagination, Miss Barry?

111
00:06:35.794 --> 00:06:42.218
If you do, imagine you are Diana and me We didn't know there was anybody in the bed,

112
00:06:42.678 --> 00:06:44.339
and we nearly died!

113
00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.961
And we couldn't sleep in the guest room.

114
00:06:47.662 --> 00:06:50.143
You're probably used to staying in a guest room.

115
00:06:50.784 --> 00:06:55.787
But imagine you're a little orphan girl who's never stayed in a guest room."

116
00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:58.589
Miss Barry actually laughed.

117
00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.072
Diana, listening outside, was relieved.

118
00:07:02.092 --> 00:07:06.795
"My imagination is a little rusty," Miss Barry said.

119
00:07:07.916 --> 00:07:10.298
"But sit down and tell me about yourself."

120
00:07:10.318 --> 00:07:15.343
"I'm very sorry, but I can't," said Anne.

121
00:07:15.363 --> 00:07:19.346
"I would like to because you seem like an interesting lady.

122
00:07:19.947 --> 00:07:23.850
You might even be a kindred spirit, though you don't look like one.

123
00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.953
I must go home to Miss Marilla Cuthbert.

124
00:07:27.533 --> 00:07:30.436
She is a very kind lady who is bringing me up.

125
00:07:31.076 --> 00:07:34.920
But before I go, please say you forgive Diana and me."

126
00:07:35.684 --> 00:07:41.627
"If you come and talk to me sometimes, I will forgive you both," Miss Barry said.

127
00:07:43.368 --> 00:07:50.412
That evening Miss Barry gave Diana a silver bracelet and decided not to return to Charlottetown.

128
00:07:50.432 --> 00:07:56.676
"I'm staying in Avonlea so I can get acquainted with Anne," she said frankly.

129
00:07:56.696 --> 00:08:03.680
"She amuses me, and at my age, an amusing person is a rarity."

130
00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.766
Miss Barry stayed for more than a month, and she and Anne became firm friends.

131
00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:15.512
Anne confided to Marilla, "Miss Barry was a kindred spirit, after all!"
